WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.044 --> 00:00:03.044
(audience cheering)

00:00:05.012 --> 00:00:09.572
- [Kelly] We've got some
fans. We got got a few fans.

00:00:09.572 --> 00:00:10.419
- Thank you!

00:00:10.419 --> 00:00:13.649
(audience wooing)

00:00:13.649 --> 00:00:16.140
- I mean, I swear to God
don't think Harry Styles

00:00:16.140 --> 00:00:17.347
gets that kind of entrance here.

00:00:17.347 --> 00:00:18.658
That was amazing!

00:00:18.658 --> 00:00:19.491
Did you-

00:00:19.491 --> 00:00:21.386
- Harry Style doesn't hang
out in the parking lot.

00:00:21.386 --> 00:00:22.770
(Kelly and Gabriel laughs)

00:00:22.770 --> 00:00:24.499
- I love a good tailgate. So I'm there.

00:00:24.499 --> 00:00:26.490
Do you know Laura, have
y'all ever met before?

00:00:26.490 --> 00:00:27.750
- No, I thought I thought it was so cool

00:00:27.750 --> 00:00:30.670
the fact that we both said
it's nice to meet sincere,

00:00:30.670 --> 00:00:31.503
like wow.
- Yeah.

00:00:31.503 --> 00:00:32.336
- It was like, so cool.

00:00:32.336 --> 00:00:34.305
- Yeah. You're both very kind.

00:00:34.305 --> 00:00:35.138
- Thank you.

00:00:35.138 --> 00:00:36.739
- Yes. So wait, this is huge.

00:00:36.739 --> 00:00:38.790
So, you're the first
comedian to ever do standup

00:00:38.790 --> 00:00:39.623
at Dodger Stadium.

00:00:39.623 --> 00:00:40.456
First of all,

00:00:40.456 --> 00:00:41.664
I said to her up for email,

00:00:41.664 --> 00:00:43.480
I was like, doing Dodger
Stadium, that's amazing.

00:00:43.480 --> 00:00:44.894
You know people fit in there?

00:00:44.894 --> 00:00:45.727
(audience cheering)

00:00:45.727 --> 00:00:47.227
That's incredible.

00:00:48.809 --> 00:00:50.330
Are you freaking out?

00:00:50.330 --> 00:00:51.560
- It's very surreal

00:00:51.560 --> 00:00:53.900
because I've been to the
ballpark a million times,

00:00:53.900 --> 00:00:55.140
been going there since I was a kid.

00:00:55.140 --> 00:00:57.180
And so the fact that
this show's gonna happen

00:00:57.180 --> 00:00:59.000
it's the biggest thing I've ever done.

00:00:59.000 --> 00:00:59.833
And it's at home.

00:00:59.833 --> 00:01:00.976
- [Laura] Isn't that amazing?
(audience cheering)

00:01:00.976 --> 00:01:01.994
- I know, that's so cool!

00:01:01.994 --> 00:01:06.530
Do you get excited about home
crowds or do you get nervous?

00:01:06.530 --> 00:01:08.410
- I used to get really
nervous about home shows

00:01:08.410 --> 00:01:10.050
'cause then you get the phone calls,

00:01:10.050 --> 00:01:11.240
'Hey man. What's up?'

00:01:11.240 --> 00:01:13.229
People I haven't heard
from all year, you know?

00:01:13.229 --> 00:01:14.630
(speaking foreign language)

00:01:14.630 --> 00:01:16.947
I'm like, 'great. I
gotta hook up tickets'.

00:01:16.947 --> 00:01:18.551
(Kelly laughs)
Right?

00:01:18.551 --> 00:01:20.110
And then just people coming up

00:01:20.110 --> 00:01:21.080
that I haven't seen in a long time.

00:01:21.080 --> 00:01:22.300
So it's a little extra pressure.

00:01:22.300 --> 00:01:25.150
- Do you say ticketmaster.com? (laughs)

00:01:25.150 --> 00:01:25.983
- [Gabriel] Nice.

00:01:25.983 --> 00:01:27.692
- [Kelly] Do you send them there?

00:01:27.692 --> 00:01:28.525
- Well, first of all,

00:01:28.525 --> 00:01:30.950
with Mexican families it's
hard because they guilt you.

00:01:30.950 --> 00:01:31.783
- Yeah.

00:01:31.783 --> 00:01:32.675
- Somebody know what I'm talking-

00:01:32.675 --> 00:01:33.580
- [Woman In Audience] Yeah!

00:01:33.580 --> 00:01:34.580
- I think you don't have to be Mexican.

00:01:34.580 --> 00:01:35.520
All families will.

00:01:35.520 --> 00:01:36.441
There's a level of guilt happening.

00:01:36.441 --> 00:01:37.350
Yes.

00:01:37.350 --> 00:01:39.425
- But they bring in
religion and your childhood.

00:01:39.425 --> 00:01:40.258
(audience laughs)

00:01:40.258 --> 00:01:41.091
- Oh. So does Southern Baptists.

00:01:41.091 --> 00:01:43.510
- [Gabriel] Oh, okay. (laughs)

00:01:43.510 --> 00:01:45.570
- Like all religious people
can bring that in there.

00:01:45.570 --> 00:01:48.630
Dodger Stadium holds tens
of thousands of people.

00:01:48.630 --> 00:01:49.463
And here you are,

00:01:49.463 --> 00:01:52.060
in the early days performing
for around 10 people.

00:01:52.060 --> 00:01:53.173
- [Gabriel] Oh wow.

00:01:53.173 --> 00:01:55.780
- [Kelly] You've come a long way.

00:01:55.780 --> 00:01:57.590
Since, when I said, that's amazing.

00:01:57.590 --> 00:01:58.423
- [Gabriel] Oh man.

00:01:58.423 --> 00:01:59.420
- [Kelly] Do you remember
these kind of shows?

00:01:59.420 --> 00:02:00.253
- [Gabriel] I try not to.

00:02:00.253 --> 00:02:01.643
(Kelly and audience laughs)

00:02:01.643 --> 00:02:04.350
- [Kelly] But these are
the ones that mold you

00:02:04.350 --> 00:02:05.832
into who you become.

00:02:05.832 --> 00:02:07.080
- Yeah.

00:02:07.080 --> 00:02:08.850
And see, I guess ignorance is bliss.

00:02:08.850 --> 00:02:11.550
Because back then you don't
know what a bad show is.

00:02:11.550 --> 00:02:12.480
You don't know-
- Yeah no.

00:02:12.480 --> 00:02:13.960
- No bad moments or situations.

00:02:13.960 --> 00:02:15.180
Cause you haven't been around long enough

00:02:15.180 --> 00:02:16.400
you're just happy to be working.

00:02:16.400 --> 00:02:17.390
And so when someone says,

00:02:17.390 --> 00:02:20.180
'you wanna perform and hold
a microphone next to a pool?'

00:02:20.180 --> 00:02:21.013
- [Kelly] Sure.

00:02:21.013 --> 00:02:21.846
- Yeah. Why not?

00:02:21.846 --> 00:02:22.679
Yeah. Let let's do.

00:02:22.679 --> 00:02:23.521
If I would've dropped that,

00:02:23.521 --> 00:02:24.846
(Gabriel and Kelly laughs)

00:02:24.846 --> 00:02:25.780
- It's over.

00:02:25.780 --> 00:02:28.343
- Let's get electricity as
close to the water as possible.

00:02:28.343 --> 00:02:29.176
(audience laughing)

00:02:29.176 --> 00:02:30.550
I've done shows in backyards,

00:02:30.550 --> 00:02:32.010
off of the back of pickup trucks,

00:02:32.010 --> 00:02:33.830
inside of empty swimming pools,

00:02:33.830 --> 00:02:35.611
because the guy said it
was good for acoustics.

00:02:35.611 --> 00:02:36.920
(audience laughs)

00:02:36.920 --> 00:02:37.844
- Well-
- Yeah right.

00:02:37.844 --> 00:02:38.677
- I don't know if he's wrong there.

00:02:38.677 --> 00:02:39.510
- Meanwhile it looks
like I'm going to fight

00:02:39.510 --> 00:02:40.343
Van Damme down there.
You know what I mean?

00:02:40.343 --> 00:02:41.176
It's all empty.

00:02:41.176 --> 00:02:42.009
There's still water.

00:02:42.009 --> 00:02:45.140
- Fight Van Damme. (laughs)

00:02:45.140 --> 00:02:46.680
I will say though, one of my first gigs,

00:02:46.680 --> 00:02:48.210
I sing at a wrestling match,

00:02:48.210 --> 00:02:49.043
the National Anthem,

00:02:49.043 --> 00:02:50.433
but I didn't know what
wrestling was really,

00:02:51.966 --> 00:02:53.760
or what that was gonna look like.

00:02:53.760 --> 00:02:55.560
And so I borrowed a friend's dress

00:02:55.560 --> 00:02:57.420
and it was a really
nice black, long dress.

00:02:57.420 --> 00:02:59.528
Like I was going to
like prom or something.

00:02:59.528 --> 00:03:00.361
- Yeah.

00:03:00.361 --> 00:03:03.593
- And I was whoa fish out of water.

00:03:05.227 --> 00:03:08.950
I was ready to feel like Whitney Houston,

00:03:08.950 --> 00:03:10.940
and all these other people
were like in tank tops.

00:03:10.940 --> 00:03:12.290
Have you ever had that happen with work,

00:03:12.290 --> 00:03:13.123
like in the audition-

00:03:13.123 --> 00:03:13.956
- Oh yeah, all the time.

00:03:13.956 --> 00:03:14.980
When you're overdressed or underdressed.

00:03:14.980 --> 00:03:17.723
And everyone else got
the memo and you didn't.

00:03:17.723 --> 00:03:20.521
You might as well be standing
there in a chicken suit.

00:03:20.521 --> 00:03:21.354
- Wow.

00:03:21.354 --> 00:03:22.187
(Gabriel laughing)

00:03:22.187 --> 00:03:23.994
I've actually been in
a chicken suit party.

00:03:23.994 --> 00:03:25.331
(Kelly and Gabriel laughs)

00:03:25.331 --> 00:03:27.053
So, it's a true story.

00:03:28.380 --> 00:03:29.213
So here you are,

00:03:29.213 --> 00:03:30.046
- $20 is $20.

00:03:30.046 --> 00:03:30.879
- You know what?

00:03:30.879 --> 00:03:31.712
(all laughs)

00:03:31.712 --> 00:03:33.604
You know what? I was
trying to win a contest.

00:03:33.604 --> 00:03:36.040
So here you are with your first check

00:03:36.040 --> 00:03:37.550
for doing a comedy show.

00:03:37.550 --> 00:03:38.556
Look at your little face!

00:03:38.556 --> 00:03:39.822
(audience cheering)

00:03:39.822 --> 00:03:40.766
- [Gabriel] Oh.

00:03:40.766 --> 00:03:41.599
- [Kelly] Your little
face with your a braces.

00:03:41.599 --> 00:03:42.760
I love you!

00:03:42.760 --> 00:03:43.640
- Oh my God. Yeah.

00:03:43.640 --> 00:03:46.120
- It's $435, 79 cents.

00:03:46.120 --> 00:03:48.280
So what show was that for?

00:03:48.280 --> 00:03:51.350
- It was for my first
television show appearance

00:03:51.350 --> 00:03:54.590
on Comedy Central's show
called 'Make Me Laugh'.

00:03:54.590 --> 00:03:56.700
And I did the show and
when I got the check,

00:03:56.700 --> 00:03:59.150
I'm like, 'it took me two
minutes to make this'.

00:03:59.150 --> 00:04:00.770
And then my head, I did the ghetto math

00:04:00.770 --> 00:04:01.790
where I'm like,

00:04:01.790 --> 00:04:02.623
- [Kelly] Ghetto math.

00:04:02.623 --> 00:04:03.456
- Ghetto math where I'm like,

00:04:03.456 --> 00:04:04.289
'if I did this for eight hours,

00:04:04.289 --> 00:04:05.950
how much, you just start
having those fantasies-

00:04:05.950 --> 00:04:06.783
- Yes.

00:04:06.783 --> 00:04:07.616
- Of-

00:04:07.616 --> 00:04:08.449
- Yes.

00:04:08.449 --> 00:04:09.353
(audience cheering)
Yes.

00:04:10.430 --> 00:04:12.840
- Do you remember the
first thing you bought

00:04:12.840 --> 00:04:15.350
with your first professional money?

00:04:15.350 --> 00:04:16.183
Do you remember what-

00:04:16.183 --> 00:04:17.016
- That right there, yes.

00:04:17.016 --> 00:04:17.849
And I still have it.

00:04:17.849 --> 00:04:20.080
A leather jacket from
Wilson's House of Suede.

00:04:20.080 --> 00:04:21.830
- I bought a coat. I bought a coat.

00:04:22.969 --> 00:04:24.480
I remember that. Yeah.

00:04:24.480 --> 00:04:26.860
- It had the liner with the zipper, right?

00:04:26.860 --> 00:04:28.033
And then it had the thing-

00:04:28.033 --> 00:04:29.010
- [Kelly] Oh. Where you
could take the, yes!

00:04:29.010 --> 00:04:30.440
Oh, it was bad. I still got it.

00:04:30.440 --> 00:04:31.300
- [Kelly] Fancy.

00:04:31.300 --> 00:04:32.169
- Still fits too. What?

00:04:32.169 --> 00:04:33.002
- Fancy.

00:04:33.002 --> 00:04:36.002
(audience cheering)

00:04:37.170 --> 00:04:39.760
- I was remembering something
I bought and I was like,

00:04:39.760 --> 00:04:43.020
'well that's yesteryear.
Can't fit into that.'

00:04:43.020 --> 00:04:46.790
So do you remember your
first acting paid gig though?

00:04:46.790 --> 00:04:49.010
- I was an understudy for a play called

00:04:49.010 --> 00:04:50.870
'Six Degrees Of Separation'.

00:04:50.870 --> 00:04:52.610
Out of school, which was a Broadway show.

00:04:52.610 --> 00:04:53.540
That was amazing.

00:04:53.540 --> 00:04:55.518
I was the happiest understudy ever.

00:04:55.518 --> 00:04:57.143
Like most understudies were sort of like,

00:04:57.143 --> 00:04:58.840
'yeah, I'll never going on',

00:04:58.840 --> 00:05:00.374
but I loved it.

00:05:00.374 --> 00:05:02.630
I would sit in the catwalk,

00:05:02.630 --> 00:05:05.230
I would sit way up high and watch a show.

00:05:05.230 --> 00:05:06.250
I loved it to pieces.

00:05:06.250 --> 00:05:07.083
Yep.

00:05:07.083 --> 00:05:07.916
- I love that.

00:05:07.916 --> 00:05:08.950
I love those moments too,

00:05:11.085 --> 00:05:12.520
where I still get excited.

00:05:12.520 --> 00:05:13.830
I hope I never get jaded like that.

00:05:13.830 --> 00:05:14.953
You know, you're run into
people that get jaded.

00:05:14.953 --> 00:05:16.619
- Oh it's only.
(audience laughs)

00:05:16.619 --> 00:05:17.452
- [Kelly] Yeah. Yeah.

00:05:17.452 --> 00:05:18.990
- And I don't know where
the accent came from

00:05:18.990 --> 00:05:20.090
but that's how I sound when I look at-

00:05:20.090 --> 00:05:22.478
- I love that she becomes an old smoker

00:05:22.478 --> 00:05:23.960
and then you, (laughs)

00:05:23.960 --> 00:05:24.793
- I become British.

00:05:24.793 --> 00:05:25.720
You become an old British man. Really.

00:05:25.720 --> 00:05:29.429
- I say. They're trying
to pay me in pesos.

00:05:29.429 --> 00:05:33.038
(Kelly and audience laughs)

00:05:33.038 --> 00:05:34.371
- British pesos.

